If using ACLs in Consul, you'll need appropriate permissions. For Consul 0.8,
the following will work for most use-cases, assuming that your service name is
`vault` and the prefix being used is `vault/`:

```json
{
  "key": {
    "vault/": {
      "policy": "write"
    }
  },
  "service": {
    "vault": {
      "policy": "write"
    }
  },
  "agent": {
    "": {
      "policy": "read"
    }
  },
  "session": {
    "": {
      "policy": "write"
    }
  }
}
```

